---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Digital Product License"
  description="Plenivostudio single-user license terms: what you may do with purchased digital products and what is not permitted."
  path="/license"
>
  <section class="section-tight legal">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 780px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Digital Product License</h1>

      <p class="muted">Last updated: October 2026.</p>

      <h2>What you get</h2>
      <p>
        When you purchase a Plenivostudio product, you receive a <strong>single-user,
        non-exclusive, non-transferable license</strong> to use the product files.
        "Single user" means you, the purchaser, as one individual.
      </p>

      <h2>Permitted uses</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the planner on any devices you personally own and use.</li>
        <li>Keep backup copies of the files for your own archival purposes.</li>
        <li>
          Export your own planning data and move it between your devices.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Not permitted</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Sharing, uploading, redistributing or reselling the product files.</li>
        <li>Publishing the files or substantial parts of them publicly.</li>
        <li>Transferring your license to another person.</li>
        <li>Using the product to build a competing redistributable product.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Ownership</h2>
      <p>
        The license grants use, not ownership. All intellectual property rights in
        the software remain with Plenivostudio.
      </p>

      <h2>Updates</h2>
      <p>
        A one-time purchase covers the version you bought. If we release a new
        major version, it may be sold separately — we will never silently convert
        your purchase into a subscription or paywall features you already bought.
      </p>

      <h2>Termination</h2>
      <p>
        If you materially breach this license (for example by redistributing the
        files), your license terminates. Files already in your possession for
        personal use are unaffected by termination of future update eligibility,
        but you must stop any infringing distribution.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
